            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0182" n="84" xml:id="pg84"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-29T12:00:00+08:00">January 29,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 30—6:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>89. My January 25, 3 p.m.</p>
                <p>1. Following from American Consul General at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“January 27, 3 p.m. The substance of your January 25, 3 p.m., has been
                            telegraphed to Bishop O’Shea at Kanchow with my full concurrence in
                            recommendation made.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>2. Following from Ministry of Foreign Affairs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Ministry of Foreign Affairs begs to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                            Hewes’ telegram dated 25th and to inform him that Kiating [<hi
                                rendition="#italic">Kiangsi?</hi>] provincial authorities have been
                            telegraphically requested to afford necessary protection to Americans in
                            Kanchow.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Chargé:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Hewes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
